// The attach link's origin (DESIGN-COMPUTE §7.10, §12.5, D-HARN-6; HARN-M14-01): the statement a caller's sidecar signs
// before an exec of ur harness rpc, which the receiving SSH server verifies outside the agents' container and hands the
// Harness as the session's verified header, and the origin each command carries. It is the body of a §6.9 Signed of
// purpose attach-origin and type SIGNED_ATTACH_ORIGIN (0x1808, §6.11, Appendix D), by the caller's identity key, over
// the session's own exchange hash, so no origin moves to another session or is chosen by a line's writer. The
// statement rides only in an origin@ur.io request on a session of the bundled SSH, over a Required overlay connection
// between a member's sidecar and its enclave (§12, IC-2), and a stamped line's origin rides inside that session as JSON
// (harness_rpc.go), so no server reads a field.

